{"pk": "1252", "sid": "PKDB00768", "name": "Biollaz1982", "licence": "open", "access": "public", "date": "2024-04-24", "group_count": 3, "individual_count": 0, "intervention_count": 2, "output_count": 236, "output_calculated_count": 12, "subset_count": 3, "timecourse_count": 3, "scatter_count": 0, "reference": {"pk": 1259, "study": {"sid": "PKDB00768", "name": "Biollaz1982"}, "pmid": "6289859", "sid": "6289859", "name": "Biollaz1982", "doi": "10.1111/j.1365-2125.1982.tb01992.x", "title": "Enalapril maleate and a lysine analogue (MK-521) in normal volunteers; relationship between plasma drug levels and the renin angiotensin system.", "abstract": "1 Two single doses of 10 mg each of the converting enzyme inhibitor enalapril maleate or MK-421 and of its lysine analogue (MK-521) were administered p.o. to twelve male volunteers. 2 The active diacid metabolite of MK-421 and the lysine analogue were determined by radioimmunoassay and MK-421 by the active metabolite method following in vitro hydrolysis. 3 Peak serum levels of MK-421, active metabolite and lysine analogue were reached within 1, 3 to 4, and 6 h respectively. Practically all MK-421 had disappeared from serum within 4 h. 4 A close correlation between percent inhibition of plasma converting enzyme activity and the serum concentration of active metabolite was observed ( r = 0.98, n = 171, P less than 0.001). Similarly, converting enzyme blockade as expressed by the ratio plasma angiotensin II/angiotensin I was closely correlated with serum active metabolite levels (r = 0.93, n = 15, P less than 0.001).", "journal": "British journal of clinical pharmacology", "date": "1982-12-16", "authors": [{"pk": 7246, "first_name": "J", "last_name": "Biollaz"}, {"pk": 7247, "first_name": "J L", "last_name": "Schelling"}, {"pk": 7248, "first_name": "B", "last_name": "Jacot Des Combes"}, {"pk": 7249, "first_name": "D B", "last_name": "Brunner"}, {"pk": 7250, "first_name": "G", "last_name": "Desponds"}, {"pk": 7251, "first_name": "H R", "last_name": "Brunner"}, {"pk": 7252, "first_name": "E H", "last_name": "Ulm"}, {"pk": 7253, "first_name": "M", "last_name": "Hichens"}, {"pk": 7254, "first_name": "H J", "last_name": "Gomez"}]}, "reference_date": "1982-12-16", "creator": {"username": "shubhankarpalwankar", "first_name": "Shubhankar", "last_name": "Palwankar"}, "curators": [{"rating": 3.0, "username": "shubhankarpalwankar", "first_name": "Shubhankar", "last_name": "Palwankar"}, {"rating": 0.0, "username": "mkoenig", "first_name": "Matthias", "last_name": "K\u00f6nig"}], "collaborators": [], "comments": [], "descriptions": [{"pk": 4598, "text": "In short, twelve normotensive male volunteers aged 22 to 33 years were included in the study"}, {"pk": 4599, "text": "On the morning of day 1, the volunteers came to the hospital outpatient department at 07.00 h after an overnight fast"}, {"pk": 4600, "text": "A resting period of 30 min"}, {"pk": 4601, "text": "Two single doses of 10 mg each of the converting enzyme inhibitor enalapril maleate or MK-421 and of its lysine analogue (MK-521) were administered"}, {"pk": 4602, "text": "blood samples for the measurement of plasma converting enzyme activity and drug levels were drawn immediately prior to drug administration at 08.00 h (time 0) and 15, 30, 60 and 90 min, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 10, 24, 48, 72 h later"}, {"pk": 4603, "text": "blood samples for the measurement of plasma angiotensin I and II were drawn at times 0, 1, 4, 10 and 24 h in six subjects after MK-421 as well as in six subjects after the lysine analogue MK-521"}], "files": [{"pk": 15130, "name": "data/Biollaz1982_Fig1.png", "file": "/media/data/Biollaz1982_Fig1.png"}, {"pk": 15129, "name": "data/.Biollaz1982_Fig1.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Biollaz1982_Fig1.tsv"}, {"pk": 15133, "name": "data/Biollaz1982_Fig2.png", "file": "/media/data/Biollaz1982_Fig2.png"}, {"pk": 15127, "name": "data/.Biollaz1982_Fig2.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Biollaz1982_Fig2.tsv"}, {"pk": 15131, "name": "data/Biollaz1982_F